Subject: Welcome to nbbbenuts - Belgian geographic code converter
From: Romain Grailet <romain.grailet@gmail.com>
To:
X-Unsent: 1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/html; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"></head>
<body style="margin:0; padding:24px; background:#f4f5f7;">
  <div style="max-width:640px; margin:0 auto; background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:10px; padding:32px 36px; font-family:-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; color:#1f2328; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">

    <p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Hi,</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 16px;">
      Welcome, and thanks for trying <strong>nbbbenuts</strong> &mdash; an R package to
      convert Belgian geographic codes between classification systems (NIS
      communes / districts / provinces / regions, NUTS, postal) and across time
      versions (NIS&nbsp;BEFORE_2019 / 2019 / 2025, NUTS&nbsp;2021 / 2027).
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:28px 0 10px; font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:#111827; border-bottom:1px solid #eaecef; padding-bottom:6px;">
      Get started
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
      The package lives here:
      <a href="https://github.com/N0n3Z/RegionalClassification" style="color:#2563eb; text-decoration:none;">
        github.com/N0n3Z/RegionalClassification</a>
    </p>

    <pre style="margin:0 0 12px; background:#f6f8fa; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:8px; padding:14px 16px; font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,Menlo,monospace; font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.5; color:#24292f; overflow-x:auto; white-space:pre;"><span style="color:#6a737d;"># install.packages("remotes")</span>
remotes::install_github(<span style="color:#032f62;">"N0n3Z/RegionalClassification"</span>)

<span style="color:#d73a49;">library</span>(nbbbenuts)
master_data &lt;- load_master_data()</pre>

    <p style="margin:0 0 16px;">
      The README has a Quick Start, and <code style="background:#eef1f4; padding:1px 5px; border-radius:4px; font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,Menlo,monospace; font-size:13px;">demo/demo.R</code>
      walks through every function.
      <em style="color:#57606a;">(Note: the repository is private, so you'll need access &mdash; reply to me
      if <code style="background:#eef1f4; padding:1px 5px; border-radius:4px; font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,Menlo,monospace; font-size:13px;">install_github</code> asks you to authenticate.)</em>
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:28px 0 10px; font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:#111827; border-bottom:1px solid #eaecef; padding-bottom:6px;">
      Sharing the package
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 16px;">
      Feel free to pass it along! If you do, just ask the new user to
      <strong>forward this email with me in CC</strong>
      (<a href="mailto:romain.grailet@gmail.com" style="color:#2563eb; text-decoration:none;">romain.grailet@gmail.com</a>).
      That way I can keep track of who's using the package and keep everyone in
      the loop on updates.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:28px 0 10px; font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:#111827; border-bottom:1px solid #eaecef; padding-bottom:6px;">
      Heads-up: this is a work in progress
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 16px;">
      The package is still under active development, so you'll probably run into
      bugs or rough edges. That's expected &mdash; and <strong>any feedback is very
      welcome</strong>: bugs, confusing behaviour, missing conversions, feature
      ideas, anything. Just reply to this email or open an issue on GitHub.
    </p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 4px;">Thanks, and happy converting!</p>
    <p style="margin:16px 0 0;">Best,<br>Romain</p>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
